]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Migas (\"crumbs\" in English) is a dish traditionally made from stale bread and other ingredients in Spanish and Portuguese cuisines. Originally introduced by shepherds, migas are very popular across the Iberian Peninsula, and are the typical breakfast of hunters at monterías in some regions of Spain."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-migas"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Migas"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Andalusian cuisine","cuisine/andalusian-cuisine"],["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Spain on a Fork","ref":"site/spainonafork-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spainonafork.com","note":"Albert Bevia's video channel and site of traditional and everyday Spanish recipes.","url":"https://spainonafork.com/welcome2/","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"}]},{"h":"More from Andalusian cuisine","links":[["Ajoblanco","dish/ajoblanco"],["Chicharrón","dish/chicharron"],["Gachas","dish/gachas"],["Gazpachuelo","dish/gazpachuelo"],["Porra antequerana","dish/porra-antequerana"],["Puchero","dish/puchero"],["Tocino de cielo","dish/tocino-de-cielo"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/ba/Migas.PNG/500px-Migas.PNG","w":500,"h":367,"by":"Nanow jesús madrid 21:40, 6 May 2007 (UTC)","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Migas.PNG"}},"dish/pastiera":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pastiera","n":"Pastiera","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Neapolitan cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Pastiera or pastiera napoletana is a type of Neapolitan tart made with cooked wheat, eggs and ricotta cheese, and flavored with orange flower water. It is usually eaten at Easter."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pastiera"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastiera"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Neapolitan cuisine","cuisine/neapolitan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Lard","ingredient/lard"],["Ricotta","ingredient/ricotta"],["Wheat","ingredient/wheat"]]},{"h":"More from Neapolitan cuisine","links":[["Casatiello","dish/casatiello"],["Crocchè","dish/crocche"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/04/Pastiera_Napoletana.JPG/500px-Pastiera_Napoletana.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Mattia Luigi Nappi (Mattia Luigi Nappi)","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pastiera_Napoletana.JPG"}},"dish/shchi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/shchi","n":"Shchi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Russian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Shchi is a Russian-style cabbage soup. When sauerkraut is used instead, the soup is called sour shchi, while soups based on sorrel, spinach, nettle, and similar plants are called green shchi (Russian: зелёные щи, IPA: [zʲɪˈlʲɵnɨje ɕːi]). In the past, the term sour shchi was also used to refer to a drink, a variation of kvass, which was unrelated to the soup."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-shchi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shchi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Sauerkraut","ingredient/sauerkraut"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olga's Flavor Factory","ref":"site/olgasflavorfactory-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"olgasflavorfactory.com","note":"Russian-born home cook Olga's blog, with a dedicated Russian recipes category.","url":"https://www.olgasflavorfactory.com/category/russianrecipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Russian cuisine","links":[["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Cabbage soup","dish/cabbage-soup"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Chicken Kiev","dish/chicken-kiev"],["Chrain","dish/chrain"],["Dressed herring","dish/dressed-herring"],["Forshmak","dish/forshmak"],["Goulash","dish/goulash"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Karelian pasty","dish/karelian-pasty"],["Kasha","dish/kasha"],["Khrenovina sauce","dish/khrenovina-sauce"],["Kolach (bread)","dish/kolach-bread"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Medovukha","dish/medovukha"],["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"],["Mors (drink)","dish/mors-drink"],["Nesselrode pudding","dish/nesselrode-pudding"],["Okroshka","dish/okroshka"],["Olivier salad","dish/olivier-salad"],["Pancake","dish/pancake"],["Paska (bread)","dish/paska-bread"],["Pâté","dish/pate"],["Pelmeni","dish/pelmeni"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Pirozhki","dish/pirozhki"],["Polonaise sauce","dish/polonaise-sauce"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Pozharsky cutlet","dish/pozharsky-cutlet"],["Rassolnik","dish/rassolnik"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"],["Soured milk","dish/soured-milk"],["Syrniki","dish/syrniki"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/4a/Schi.jpg/500px-Schi.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Шнапс","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schi.jpg"}}}